  "ticker": "AAPL",
  "status": "success",
  "report": "This report is for educational use only and is not financial advice. MCP returned a successful FCFF valuation for Apple Inc. in USD using a THREE_STAGE, 15-year projection. Modeled value per share is $101.18, versus the MCP market price input of $308.82. Growth assumptions use 3.38% revenue growth for years 2-5, with a Damodaran Computers/Peripherals growth anchor showing 2026 p25/p50/p75 proxies of 3.55%, 6.79%, and 10.36% at 0.61 confidence. Margins start from a 32.64% base-year operating margin, use 33.00% next year, and converge to a 25.27% target by year 10. Reinvestment is driven by sales-to-capital of 3.68x in years 1-5 and 2.74x in years 6-10; terminal reinvestment rate is 47.76%. Cost of capital starts at 9.13% and reaches 9.63% in the terminal year, using a 4.60% risk-free rate plus Damodaran mature-market and country equity risk premium inputs. Terminal assumptions are 4.60% growth, 9.63% cost of capital, $84.97B terminal cash flow, $1.689T terminal value, and $446.02B present value of terminal value. Data caveats: rates are percentages, sales-to-capital is a multiple, market expectation checks solve one variable at a time, and market data comes from Yahoo Finance through the local yfinance service, which can be missing, stale, or insufficient for some companies."
}
